WEBVTT

00:02.258 --> 00:04.427
KATARA: Water.

00:04.844 --> 00:06.304
Earth.

00:06.596 --> 00:08.598
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:10.308
Air.

00:11.142 --> 00:15.104
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.438 --> 00:19.275
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.776 --> 00:22.403
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.529 --> 00:23.738
could stop them.

00:23.863 --> 00:26.699
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.367 --> 00:29.494
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.577 --> 00:32.664
the new Avatar, an airbender named Aang.

00:32.956 --> 00:35.166
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.291 --> 00:37.585
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.710 --> 00:38.920
AANG: Oof!

00:39.045 --> 00:42.006
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:58.136 --> 01:00.681
Hey, I remember her.
She helped you attack us.

01:01.390 --> 01:03.392
Yep. Back in the good old days.

01:04.810 --> 01:06.937
JUNE: Oh, great, it's Prince Pouty.

01:07.062 --> 01:08.271
Where's your creepy grandpa?

01:08.522 --> 01:11.191
He's my uncle. And he's not here.

01:12.109 --> 01:14.194
I see you worked things
out with your girlfriend.

01:14.361 --> 01:16.363
- I'm not his girlfriend!
- She's not my girlfriend!

01:16.738 --> 01:20.742
Okay, okay, sheesh. I was only teasing.

01:20.867 --> 01:22.119
So what do you want?

01:22.244 --> 01:24.121
I need your help finding the Avatar.

01:24.246 --> 01:26.581
Hmm, doesn't sound too fun.

01:28.166 --> 01:31.044
Does the end of the world
sound like more fun?

01:31.253 --> 01:33.171
( BOTH GROWLING )

01:33.296 --> 01:35.132
( SLURPING )

01:37.718 --> 01:39.261
Nyla?

01:39.886 --> 01:41.638
( CHOMPING )

01:41.763 --> 01:45.100
Whose my little snuffly-wuffly?

01:45.225 --> 01:47.269
Whoa! Careful there!

01:47.394 --> 01:50.272
Okay, so who's got something
with the Avatar's scent on it?

01:50.439 --> 01:51.898
I have Aang's staff.

01:53.859 --> 01:56.278
( SNIFFING )

01:59.698 --> 02:03.035
( SNIFFING )

02:06.163 --> 02:08.498
( SNIFFING )

02:09.708 --> 02:12.127
( QUIET GROWLING )

02:12.252 --> 02:14.004
Well, what does that mean?

02:14.337 --> 02:15.839
It means your friend's gone.

02:16.214 --> 02:17.674
We know he's gone.

02:17.799 --> 02:19.509
That's why we're trying to find him.

02:19.801 --> 02:21.428
No, I mean he's gone-gone.

02:21.553 --> 02:23.055
He doesn't exist.

02:27.768 --> 02:29.144
( CHATTERING )

02:29.269 --> 02:30.604
Where are we, Momo?

02:33.106 --> 02:35.150
Maybe I'm in the Spirit World?

02:37.861 --> 02:40.197
But, wait, you can see me.

02:40.322 --> 02:42.365
We could both be in the Spirit World.

02:46.787 --> 02:49.081
Nope, my bending works.

02:49.206 --> 02:51.333
Maybe if we climb to
the top of the island,

02:51.458 --> 02:53.085
we can figure out where we are.

02:54.669 --> 02:56.880
What do you mean Aang doesn't exist?

03:00.133 --> 03:02.511
Nope, we could find him if he were dead.

03:02.636 --> 03:04.346
Oh, it's a real head-scratcher.

03:04.429 --> 03:05.555
See ya.

03:06.098 --> 03:08.475
TOPH: Helpful. Real helpful.

03:08.600 --> 03:10.477
ZUKO: Wait, I have another idea.

03:11.103 --> 03:12.813
There's only one other person
in this world

03:12.938 --> 03:14.981
who can help us face the Fire Lord.

03:15.107 --> 03:17.067
I'll be right back with a smell sample.

03:17.776 --> 03:19.152
( FLIES BUZZING )

03:19.277 --> 03:21.780
You saved your uncle's sweaty sandal?

03:21.905 --> 03:23.698
I think it's kind of sweet.

03:24.783 --> 03:27.035
( SNIFFING )

03:27.160 --> 03:28.411
Let's do this.

03:31.373 --> 03:32.833
ZUKO: Hey, wait up!

03:57.816 --> 03:59.401
ZUKO: We're going to Ba Sing Se?

04:00.652 --> 04:02.487
JUNE: Your uncle is
somewhere beyond the wall.

04:02.612 --> 04:04.656
Nyla is getting twitchy,
so he can't be too far.

04:05.073 --> 04:06.658
Good luck.

04:10.745 --> 04:12.080
It's been a long day.

04:12.247 --> 04:14.207
Let's camp and start
our search again at dawn.

04:17.836 --> 04:22.507
( BIRDS TWITTERING )

04:22.632 --> 04:24.759
It's a hexagon.

04:24.885 --> 04:26.428
( CHATTERS )

04:26.553 --> 04:28.430
It doesn't seem like normal rock.

04:32.934 --> 04:34.603
It's not made of earth.

04:34.728 --> 04:36.521
This is so strange.

04:36.771 --> 04:41.026
I wish some help right now.
I wish I had Roku.

04:41.151 --> 04:43.195
I do have Roku!

04:43.320 --> 04:46.781
( BREATHING DEEPLY )

04:54.039 --> 04:55.790
You're right, Aang.

04:55.916 --> 04:58.543
All the past Avatars,

04:58.668 --> 05:03.048
all their experience and wisdom
is available to you,

05:03.340 --> 05:06.885
if you look deep inside yourself.

05:07.010 --> 05:10.180
So, where am I, Roku? What is this place?

05:10.305 --> 05:13.683
I don't know, Aang.

05:13.934 --> 05:17.812
But I see that you are lost in
more ways than one right now.

05:18.021 --> 05:19.064
I am.

05:19.189 --> 05:22.067
I need to figure out what to do
once I face the Fire Lord.

05:23.944 --> 05:25.946
SOKKA: ( SNORING )

05:26.571 --> 05:27.614
Huh?

05:32.452 --> 05:33.703
APPA: ( BELLOWING )

05:41.503 --> 05:43.505
Well, look who's here.

05:43.630 --> 05:45.340
( LAUGHS, SNORTS )

05:55.850 --> 05:58.019
Everyone expects me to
take the Fire Lord's life.

05:58.270 --> 06:00.355
But I just don't know if I can do that.

06:00.480 --> 06:05.902
In my life, I tried to be
disciplined and show restraint,

06:06.027 --> 06:08.613
but it backfired when Fire Lord Sozin

06:08.738 --> 06:12.701
took advantage of my restraint and mercy.

06:12.826 --> 06:16.830
If had been more decisive,
and acted sooner,

06:16.955 --> 06:18.790
I could have stopped Sozin

06:18.915 --> 06:22.377
and stopped the war before it started.

06:22.544 --> 06:25.297
I offer you this wisdom, Aang.

06:25.463 --> 06:28.008
You must be decisive.

06:34.848 --> 06:36.099
TOPH: What's going on?

06:36.308 --> 06:38.143
We're surrounded by old people.

06:38.310 --> 06:39.811
KATARA: Not just any old people,

06:40.061 --> 06:42.814
these are great masters
and friends of ours.

06:42.939 --> 06:44.190
Pakku.

06:44.274 --> 06:47.027
It is respectful to bow to an old master.

06:47.485 --> 06:50.905
But how about a hug
for your new grandfather?

06:51.781 --> 06:53.491
- That's so exciting!
- SOKKA: ( GASPS )

06:53.616 --> 06:55.201
You and Gran-Gran must be so happy

06:55.327 --> 06:57.203
to have found each other again.

06:57.329 --> 07:00.623
I made her a new betrothal
necklace and everything.

07:00.749 --> 07:02.834
Welcome to the family, Gramp-Gramp!

07:02.959 --> 07:05.462
You can still just call me Pakku.

07:05.879 --> 07:08.965
How about Gramp-Pakku?

07:09.382 --> 07:10.800
No.

07:10.925 --> 07:13.887
And this was Aang's
first firebending teacher.

07:14.012 --> 07:15.889
Jeong Jeong.

07:16.348 --> 07:17.807
Master Piandao.

07:17.932 --> 07:19.225
Hello, Sokka.

07:19.809 --> 07:22.145
So, wait, how do you all know each other?

07:22.270 --> 07:25.440
All old people know each other,
don't you know that?

07:25.565 --> 07:27.525
( LAUGHS, SNORTS )

07:27.650 --> 07:30.612
We're all are part of the same
ancient secret society,

07:30.737 --> 07:34.491
a group that transcends the
divisions of the four nations.

07:34.616 --> 07:36.409
The Order of the White Lotus.

07:36.826 --> 07:38.828
That's the one.

07:38.953 --> 07:41.664
The White Lotus has always
been about philosophy,

07:41.790 --> 07:43.291
and beauty, and truth.

07:44.000 --> 07:45.877
But about a month ago, a call went out

07:46.002 --> 07:48.129
that we were needed
for something important.

07:48.630 --> 07:51.549
It came from a Grand Lotus, your uncle,

07:51.841 --> 07:53.760
Iroh of the Fire Nation.

07:53.885 --> 07:55.345
Well, that's who we're looking for.

07:55.678 --> 07:57.389
Then we'll take you to him.

07:57.514 --> 08:00.350
Wait, someone's missing from your group,

08:00.475 --> 08:03.269
someone very important.

08:03.395 --> 08:05.563
Where's Momo?

08:05.688 --> 08:09.234
He's gone... And so is Aang.

08:09.359 --> 08:11.236
Oh, well, so long as they have each other,

08:11.361 --> 08:13.488
I'm sure we have nothing to worry about.

08:13.571 --> 08:14.614
Let's go!

08:14.697 --> 08:17.409
( SNORTING LAUGHTER )

08:20.161 --> 08:22.372
( CHATTERS )

08:22.497 --> 08:26.584
Avatar Kyoshi, I need your wisdom.

08:34.676 --> 08:37.137
In my day, Chin The Conqueror

08:37.262 --> 08:39.264
threatened to throw
the world out of balance.

08:41.474 --> 08:46.271
I stopped him and the world
entered a great era of peace.

08:46.729 --> 08:47.939
AANG: But you didn't really kill Chin.

08:48.064 --> 08:49.482
Technically, he fell to his own doom

08:49.607 --> 08:51.818
because he was too stubborn
to get out of the way.

08:51.943 --> 08:54.487
Personally,
I don't really see the difference.

08:54.612 --> 08:56.239
But I assure you,

08:56.364 --> 08:59.284
I would have done whatever
it took to stop Chin.

08:59.701 --> 09:02.120
I offer you this wisdom, Aang.

09:02.245 --> 09:04.581
Only justice will bring peace.

09:07.750 --> 09:09.878
I knew I shouldn't have asked Kyoshi...

09:12.630 --> 09:14.257
SOKKA: So, Bumi,
how did you end up escaping

09:14.382 --> 09:16.259
your imprisonment in Omashu?

09:16.384 --> 09:18.720
Escape? I didn't escape.

09:18.845 --> 09:20.847
Everybody else escaped.

09:21.389 --> 09:23.349
There I was, back in Omashu,

09:23.475 --> 09:26.436
waiting for just the right moment.

09:26.561 --> 09:28.062
I didn't know what or when,

09:28.188 --> 09:31.691
but I knew I'd know it when I knew it.

09:31.816 --> 09:33.776
An eclipse! That'll do it!

09:34.694 --> 09:36.571
( STRAINING )

09:44.954 --> 09:46.539
What do you think you're doing?

09:46.664 --> 09:48.166
( GRUNTS )

09:48.291 --> 09:49.959
( GRUNTS )

09:51.377 --> 09:53.213
Taking back my city.

09:53.338 --> 09:56.508
You've got no firepower,
and it's payback time!

10:13.316 --> 10:15.527
( RUMBLING )

10:31.251 --> 10:32.710
( STRAINING )

10:41.928 --> 10:43.429
( LAUGHS, SNORTS )

10:43.555 --> 10:45.348
( CHOMPING )

10:46.224 --> 10:49.894
Wow, you took back your whole
city all by yourself.

10:50.395 --> 10:52.355
BUMI: So, what about you guys?

10:52.480 --> 10:55.191
Did you do anything interesting
on the day of the eclipse?

10:56.609 --> 10:58.444
- Nah.
- No, not really.

10:59.529 --> 11:01.656
I need to look deep inside myself.

11:11.291 --> 11:13.626
I am Avatar Kuruk.

11:13.751 --> 11:15.295
When I was young,

11:15.420 --> 11:20.633
I was always a "go with the flow"
kind of Avatar.

11:20.758 --> 11:23.011
People seemed to work
out their own problems,

11:23.136 --> 11:26.264
and there was peace
and good times in the world.

11:28.349 --> 11:30.935
But then, I lost the woman I loved

11:31.060 --> 11:35.732
to Koh, the face stealer.

11:35.857 --> 11:37.442
It was my fault.

11:37.567 --> 11:40.111
If I had been more attentive
and more active,

11:40.236 --> 11:42.488
I could have saved her.

11:42.614 --> 11:46.826
Aang, you must actively
shape your own destiny,

11:46.951 --> 11:49.037
and the destiny of the world.

12:01.341 --> 12:04.761
Well, here we are.
Welcome to old people camp.

12:06.888 --> 12:09.349
Where? Where is he?

12:09.474 --> 12:11.643
Your uncle's in there, Prince Zuko.

12:22.945 --> 12:24.072
Are you okay?

12:24.197 --> 12:26.115
No, I'm not okay.

12:26.240 --> 12:28.034
My uncle hates me, I know it.

12:28.159 --> 12:31.120
He loved me and supported me
in every way he could,

12:31.245 --> 12:33.289
and I still turned against him.

12:33.414 --> 12:34.999
How can I even face him?

12:35.124 --> 12:38.252
Zuko, you're sorry
for what you did, right?

12:38.378 --> 12:39.629
More sorry than I've been about anything

12:39.754 --> 12:41.339
in my entire life.

12:41.464 --> 12:44.008
Then he'll forgive you. He will.

12:49.263 --> 12:52.684
( EXHALES )

12:53.101 --> 12:54.352
Uncle...

12:54.477 --> 12:58.398
( SNORING )

13:09.826 --> 13:11.411
AANG: All these past Avatars,

13:11.494 --> 13:13.871
they keep telling me
I'm gonna have to do it.

13:13.996 --> 13:15.957
- They don't get it.
-( CHATTERS )

13:16.082 --> 13:18.126
You're right, maybe an Air Nomad Avatar

13:18.251 --> 13:20.253
will understand where I'm coming from.

13:20.378 --> 13:22.130
( PURRS )

13:22.213 --> 13:23.631
I know you can't really talk.

13:24.090 --> 13:26.008
Pretending you can just helps me think.

13:26.134 --> 13:27.635
( CHATTERS )

13:27.760 --> 13:30.096
I'm going to pretend
I didn't pretend to hear that.

13:38.730 --> 13:41.607
I am Avatar Yangchen, young airbender.

13:42.024 --> 13:44.360
Avatar Yangchen,
the monks always taught me

13:44.485 --> 13:46.070
that all life is sacred,

13:46.195 --> 13:48.906
even the life of the tiniest spider-fly
caught in its own web.

13:49.741 --> 13:52.285
Yes, all life is sacred.

13:52.702 --> 13:54.787
I know. I'm even a vegetarian.

13:54.912 --> 13:56.581
I've always tried to solve my problems

13:56.706 --> 13:58.124
by being quick or clever,

13:58.249 --> 14:00.960
and I've only had to use
violence for necessary defense,

14:01.085 --> 14:03.671
and I've certainly never
used it to take a life.

14:03.796 --> 14:07.717
Avatar Aang, I know that
you're a gentle spirit,

14:07.842 --> 14:10.178
and the monks have taught you well,

14:10.303 --> 14:12.430
but this isn't about you.

14:12.555 --> 14:14.348
This is about the world.

14:14.474 --> 14:16.809
But the monks taught me,
that I have to detach myself

14:16.934 --> 14:19.187
from the world so my spirit could be free.

14:19.437 --> 14:23.107
Many great and wise Air Nomads
have detached themselves

14:23.232 --> 14:25.985
and achieved spiritual enlightenment.

14:26.110 --> 14:28.279
But the Avatar can never do it,

14:28.404 --> 14:31.908
because your sole duty is to the world.

14:32.033 --> 14:34.702
Here is my wisdom for you...

14:35.203 --> 14:37.580
Selfless duty calls you to sacrifice

14:37.705 --> 14:39.957
your own spiritual needs

14:40.082 --> 14:44.253
and do whatever it takes
to protect the world.

14:46.714 --> 14:49.342
( CHATTERING )

14:49.467 --> 14:51.302
I guess I don't have a choice, Momo.

14:51.427 --> 14:53.971
I have to kill the Fire Lord.

15:05.399 --> 15:07.360
( YAWNING )

15:12.031 --> 15:17.787
Uncle, I know you must have
mixed feelings about seeing me.

15:17.912 --> 15:22.667
But I want you to know
I am so, so sorry, Uncle.

15:23.292 --> 15:26.337
I am so sorry and ashamed of what I did.

15:26.462 --> 15:29.423
I don't know how I can ever
make it up to you, but I―

15:35.555 --> 15:37.765
How can you forgive me so easily?

15:37.890 --> 15:39.642
I thought you would be furious with me.

15:39.767 --> 15:43.229
I was never angry with you.

15:43.354 --> 15:47.942
I was sad, because I was
afraid you'd lost your way.

15:48.067 --> 15:50.820
I did lose my way.

15:50.945 --> 15:54.490
But you've found it again...

15:55.283 --> 15:58.077
And you did it by yourself,

15:58.202 --> 16:02.290
and I am so happy you found your way here.

16:03.207 --> 16:05.585
It wasn't that hard, Uncle.

16:05.710 --> 16:07.795
You have a pretty strong scent.

16:09.088 --> 16:10.548
( SQUEAKS )

16:11.007 --> 16:12.717
( BIRDS CALLING )

16:14.719 --> 16:16.095
( DISTANT RUMBLING )

16:16.220 --> 16:18.389
( YAWNS )

16:18.514 --> 16:20.266
( RUMBLING CONTINUES )

16:20.349 --> 16:24.437
Wait, is it just me or are
those mountains getting bigger?

16:24.687 --> 16:26.355
( CHATTERS )

16:35.323 --> 16:37.283
They're not getting larger,
they're getting closer.

16:37.408 --> 16:38.826
( CHATTERS )

16:40.953 --> 16:42.496
The whole island is moving!

16:49.086 --> 16:50.504
( CHATTERS )

17:05.561 --> 17:07.396
( GASPS )

17:07.521 --> 17:08.689
( CHATTERING )

17:08.814 --> 17:10.316
It's amazing, Momo!

17:10.441 --> 17:12.193
The biggest animal in the world!

17:12.318 --> 17:14.612
I've gotta swim around and find its face.

17:26.207 --> 17:29.210
ZUKO: Uncle, you're the only
person other than the Avatar

17:29.335 --> 17:31.963
who can possibly defeat the Father Lord.

17:32.088 --> 17:33.631
You mean the Fire Lord?

17:33.756 --> 17:35.216
That's what I just said.

17:35.341 --> 17:37.218
Hmm...

17:37.343 --> 17:38.970
We need you to come with us.

17:39.595 --> 17:41.055
No, Zuko.

17:41.180 --> 17:42.723
It won't turn out well.

17:43.099 --> 17:45.977
You can beat him
and we'll be there to help.

17:46.102 --> 17:48.521
Even if I did defeat Ozai,

17:48.646 --> 17:51.107
and I don't know that I could,

17:51.232 --> 17:53.943
it would be the wrong way to end a war.

17:54.402 --> 17:57.905
History would see it as just
more senseless violence,

17:58.030 --> 18:01.117
a brother killing a brother to grab power.

18:01.242 --> 18:03.911
The only way
for this war to end peacefully

18:04.036 --> 18:07.707
is for the Avatar to defeat the Fire Lord.

18:08.541 --> 18:10.793
And then... Then would you come and take

18:10.918 --> 18:12.503
your rightful place on the throne?

18:13.045 --> 18:16.966
No. Someone new must take the throne...

18:17.091 --> 18:22.555
An idealist with a pure heart
and unquestionable honor.

18:22.680 --> 18:25.558
It has to be you, Prince Zuko.

18:25.683 --> 18:27.643
Unquestionable honor?

18:27.768 --> 18:29.478
But I've made so many mistakes.

18:29.603 --> 18:31.981
Yes, you have.

18:32.106 --> 18:35.109
You've struggled and you've suffered,

18:35.234 --> 18:37.987
but you have always
followed your own path.

18:38.195 --> 18:40.656
You restored your own honor,

18:40.781 --> 18:45.661
and only you can restore
the honor of the Fire Nation.

18:45.786 --> 18:47.705
I'll try, Uncle.

18:48.122 --> 18:50.624
Well, what if Aang doesn't come back?

18:51.375 --> 18:55.421
Sozin's Comet is arriving
and our destinies are upon us.

18:55.546 --> 18:57.590
Aang will face the Fire Lord.

18:58.799 --> 19:01.343
When I was a boy, I had a vision

19:01.469 --> 19:04.388
that I would one day take Ba Sing Se.

19:04.847 --> 19:07.224
Only now do I see that my destiny

19:07.349 --> 19:10.519
is to take it back from the Fire Nation,

19:10.644 --> 19:14.190
so the Earth Kingdom can be free again.

19:15.024 --> 19:17.943
That's why you gathered
the members of the White Lotus.

19:18.069 --> 19:20.029
Yes.

19:20.154 --> 19:23.449
Zuko, you must return to the Fire Nation,

19:23.574 --> 19:25.534
so that when the Fire Lord falls,

19:25.659 --> 19:30.539
you can assume the throne
and restore peace and order.

19:30.664 --> 19:33.959
But Azula will be there waiting for you.

19:34.085 --> 19:35.836
I can handle Azula.

19:35.961 --> 19:39.340
Not alone. You'll need help.

19:39.465 --> 19:40.841
You're right.

19:40.925 --> 19:44.011
Katara, how would you like to
help me put Azula in her place?

19:44.428 --> 19:46.347
It would be my pleasure.

19:46.472 --> 19:48.974
What about us? What's our destiny today?

19:49.725 --> 19:51.977
What do you think it is?

19:52.103 --> 19:54.855
I think that even though
we don't know where Aang is,

19:54.980 --> 19:57.900
we need to do everything we can
to stop the airship fleet.

19:58.025 --> 20:00.486
And that means, when Aang
does face the Fire Lord,

20:00.611 --> 20:02.863
we'll be right there if he need us.

20:08.661 --> 20:10.204
Nothing runs faster over land

20:10.329 --> 20:12.957
or swims quicker than a giant eel-hound.

20:13.332 --> 20:15.167
The airship base is on a small island

20:15.292 --> 20:17.294
just off the Earth Kingdom shore.

20:17.503 --> 20:21.465
You should be able to intercept the fleet
within a day's journey.

20:21.590 --> 20:23.050
Thank you, master.

20:29.265 --> 20:32.643
So, if I'm gonna be Fire Lord
after the war's over,

20:32.726 --> 20:34.061
what are you gonna do?

20:34.186 --> 20:37.273
After I reconquer Ba Sing Se,

20:37.398 --> 20:40.067
I am going to reconquer my tea shop

20:40.192 --> 20:43.696
and I am going to play Pai Sho every day.

20:48.367 --> 20:51.954
- Goodbye, General Iroh.
- Goodbye, everyone.

20:52.079 --> 20:57.001
Today, destiny is our friend. I know it.

21:38.751 --> 21:40.753
A Lion Turtle.

21:43.923 --> 21:45.466
Maybe you can help me.

21:45.591 --> 21:48.969
Everyone, even my own past lives

21:49.094 --> 21:52.932
are expecting me to end someone's life.

21:53.057 --> 21:54.600
But I don't know if I can do it.

21:54.808 --> 21:57.770
LION TURTLE: The true mind
can weather all the lies

21:57.895 --> 22:01.315
and illusions without being lost.

22:01.565 --> 22:04.568
The true heart can tough
the poison of hatred

22:04.693 --> 22:07.112
without being harmed.

22:07.321 --> 22:11.492
Since beginningless time,
darkness thrives in the void,

22:11.617 --> 22:15.246
but always yields to purifying light.

22:25.965 --> 22:27.383
Wait for him.

22:27.508 --> 22:29.260
He will come.

22:40.479 --> 22:44.233
It's time for this world to end in fire

22:44.358 --> 22:48.612
and for a new world
to be born from the ashes.

23:21.006 --> 23:23.008
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
